<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Petrobras Feb oil output down.</title>
<headline>Brazil Petrobras Feb oil output down.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state oil monopoly Petrobras produced 856,816 barrels of oil per day (bpd) in February, down 7,000 from January's daily average, Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>Daily natural gas output stood at 26,600 cubic meters in February.</p>
<p>Petrobras' exploration and production in the Amazon was expanded, while maintenance work on a platform in the Bacia de Campos oilfield, off the coast of Rio de Janeiro, helped to reduce overall oil output.</p>
<p>((--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151))</p>
